Dark Dryad was used to sabotage the Huntik team's mission but failed to capture them by the waterfall containing the [[Nexus]]. She later was used to fight [[Elf King Oberon]], immobilizing him with her roots for [[Myrmidon]] to finish him off. After [[Wilder]]'s team were defeated, she created a forest of vines so that [[Lok Lambert]]'s [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]] could not follow them and that [[Zhalia Moon]] could not track them. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

She later was used to attack the Huntik team's speedboat and managed to defeat [[Undine|Undine the Water Spirit]] at Avalon. She was then ordered to return by [[Stack]], who planned to follow them. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

She was again used to capture [[Dante Vale]], [[Sophie Casterwill]], and [[Zhalia Moon]] at Klaus's Bookstore, but they were freed with the help of [[Cherit]] and [[Springer]]. Dark Dryad then fought with Sophie's [[Sabriel]] but was defeated by a [[Nullcurse]] spell cast by the [[Silent Soldiers]] who had bombarded the operation. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

[[File:S2E27 Oberon Myrmidon.jpg|thumb|170x170px|Dark Dryad restrains [[Elf King Oberon|Oberon]], allowing [[Myrmidon]] to take him out]]
Dark Dryad's principal ability is controlling roots and vines and using them to immobilize her opponents, allowing allies to easily take them out. Still, she can also fight directly by using her vines as a whip and quickly slashing them at her enemies. Dark Dryad is also able to use her control over plant matter for camouflage or to obscure a tactical retreat. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}{{source|Doorway to Huntik}} Due to these abilities, she is an excellent [[Titan]] for ambushing the enemy. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

